<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were steady to lower on Wednesday in line with market expectations of lower interest rates, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're expecting declines across the board by this afternoon,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>Traders said the Central Bank may ease its 16 percent overnight borrowing rate since the peso is regaining strength. The peso fell prey in recent weeks to the Asian currency turmoil caused by the weakness of the Thai baht.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 June 4		  June 3</p>
<p>    1 W		13  5/16		13  9/16</p>
<p>    2 W		12  7/16		12  1/2</p>
<p>    1 M		11  1/2		 11  1/2</p>
<p>    2 M		11  1/4		 11  5/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  1/4		 11  1/4</p>
<p>    6 M		11  1/16		11  1/8</p>
<p>    12M		11  1/16		11  1/16</p>
<p>    VAL		5-Jun		   4-Jun</p>
<p>-- Lilian Karunungan (63 2) 841-8937</p>
